{
  "title": "Huly Platform \u2014 productivity (25,995\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Huly Platform\nDomain: productivity | Scale: large | Stars: 25,995\nProblem: A robust framework for accelerating development of business applications, providing an all-in-one alternative to fragmented tools like Linear, Jira, Slack, Notion, and Motion for project management, CRM, HR, and team collaboration.\nTarget users: Enterprise teams, Project managers, HR professionals, CRM users, Developers building business applications, Self-hosted deployment teams\nCore features: Project Management & Issue Tracking; Team Chat & Communication; CRM System; Human Resources Management (HRM); Applicant Tracking System (ATS); Wiki & Knowledge Base; Quality Management System (QMS); Programmatic API Client for integrations\nIntegrations: Docker, GitHub Packages, Custom API Client for third-party applications\nTech stack: Svelte with TypeScript + TypeScript, Go, Rust microservices + Unknown (referenced in architecture docs) + Docker, Docker Compose\nKey libraries: TypeScript, Svelte, SCSS, Rust, Go\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure using Rush for managing multiple applications (Chat, Project Management, CRM, HRM, ATS) as cohesive platform components\n- Platform-first approach: core framework enables third-party teams (Huly, TraceX) to build applications on top, suggesting strong API and extensibility design\n- Polyglot backend architecture combining TypeScript, Go, and Rust indicates performance-critical services are separated by language choice for optimization\n- Clear versioning strategy distinguishing production (v*) from development (s*) releases with explicit self-hosting support through separate repository, showing operational maturity",
